course: dictionary
lesson: 6703
title: Oddball and informal words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words belong to everyday talk more than to school books. Oddball is one of them: it is informal, so you will hear it with friends and in stories. Look at the clues around it. «The wise approach: use the full rhyme only for /ee/, learn silent letters in groups, and keep a short list of the famous oddballs.» Here the clues about spelling rules and exceptions help you see that oddballs are the things that do not follow the usual pattern.
explain: As a noun, an oddball is a person who behaves in a strange or unusual way. As an adjective, oddball means strange or unusual, as in an oddball idea. It can sound friendly, like someone fun and different, or unkind, like someone left out. The rest of the sentence tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: Use the swap check: put a meaning in place of oddball and see if the sentence still makes sense. Stories often have an oddball character who seems strange at first and later becomes a hero.
fact: Oddball is an informal word, so it is an everyday word rather than a formal one.
fact: «Oddball» can be a noun, «an oddball», or an adjective, «oddball», as in «an oddball idea».
fact: «Oddball» means a person who behaves in a strange or unusual way, or something strange or unusual.
fact: Oddball can be friendly, meaning someone fun and different, or unkind, meaning someone left out.
fact: Being kind means not leaving people out just because they seem different.
exercise: «The wise approach: keep a short list of the famous oddballs.» In this sentence, oddballs are | Long lists of rhyming words | Famous football players | Teachers who give extra homework | *Spellings that do not follow the usual pattern
exercise: Mia says «He's such an oddball» about a boy who collects bus tickets and talks to pigeons. What does oddball mean here? | A quiet boy who sits alone at lunch | A famous football player | A round toy for playing games | *A person who behaves in a strange or unusual way
exercise: Which word is informal and means strange or unusual? | glum | *oddball | ancient | curt
test: «The class made an oddball plan for the science fair.» What does oddball mean? | Quick and easy | Wet and grey | *Strange or unusual | Very cheap
test: Why might a kind teacher not leave out an oddball in class? | *Because everyone deserves to be included, even if they seem different | Because oddballs cannot speak | Because oddballs always win the prizes | Because oddballs are always rude
exam: Is oddball formal or informal, and what does it mean as a noun? | Formal; a kind of musical instrument | Formal; a large round toy | *Informal; a person who behaves in a strange or unusual way | Informal; a loud sound at night
